 "id": "glass",
 "title": "Glass transition",
 "statement": {
  "text": "The glass–liquid transition, or glass transition, is the gradual and reversible transition in amorphous materials from a hard and relatively brittle \"glassy\" state into a viscous or \"rubbery\" state as the temperature is increased. An amorphous solid that exhibits a glass transition is called a glass. The reverse transition, achieved by supercooling a viscous liquid into the glass state, is called vitrification.",
  "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glass_transition"
 },
